SUMMARY:The Hunchback of Notre Dame
DESCRIPTION:The sweeping\, epic musical based on Victor Hugo’s timeless tale and the beloved Disney film comes to life like never before! Featuring a soaring score by Alan Menken and Stephen Schwartz\, this powerful story of love\, acceptance\, and courage will be performed in the hauntingly beautiful Vintage Church in Downtown Raleigh. In partnership with the North Carolina Master Chorale\, Theatre Raleigh is creating the expansive choir needed for this majestic\, site-specific theatrical experience—truly unforgettable from start to finish.
URL:https://unitedarts.org/calendar/the-hunchback-of-notre-dame/2026-08-21/
LOCATION:Vintage Church on Moore Square in Downtown Raleigh  118 S Person St\, Raleigh\, NC 27601\, 118 S Person St\, Raleigh\, 27601
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://unitedarts.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/hunchbacksquare.png
ORGANIZER;CN="Theatre Raleigh":MAILTO:info@theatreraleigh.com
END:VEVENT
